Stirling PDF on FenrirOS
========================

The open-source ("core") build: merge, split, convert, OCR, sign, compress
and edit PDFs in the browser. It has NO login (user accounts are in the
proprietary edition, not built here), so anyone who reaches it can use it.

Installed inert:
    dinitctl enable stirling-pdf

It listens on 127.0.0.1:8080 only (/usr/lib/stirling-pdf/run). Put an
authenticating reverse proxy in front of it, or use an SSH tunnel.
Its settings are written to /var/lib/stirling-pdf/configs/settings.yml on
first start. Analytics (PostHog, Scarf) are turned off by the run script
(SYSTEM_ENABLEANALYTICS=false).

Optional tools it uses when installed: libreoffice (office conversions),
tesseract and ocrmypdf (OCR), qpdf (repair/compress), ghostscript,
unpaper, weasyprint (HTML to PDF).
